From: OpenWrt <openwrt@example.org>
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: deepen the PSE reserve of the second 10G port

The PSE hands each egress queue a guaranteed reserve of
PSE_QUEUE_RSV_PAGES (64) pages, and everything above that is shared.  The
port/queue table gives GDM4 only two queues, so the reserve for that port
is 2 * 64 * 128 B = 16 KiB.

On the AN7581 GDM4 is the second 10G port.  At 10G, 16 KiB is about 13 us
of traffic - less than the time it takes the CPU to get scheduled on a
busy system, so a burst aimed at GDM4 is dropped although the shared pool
is mostly idle.

The queue count is a hardware property and is left alone; instead each of
GDM4's queues is given a deeper reserve, capped by what the shared pool
can actually give away.  The pool thresholds are derived as
fq_limit - all_rsv - <headroom>, so the reserve is only raised while that
subtraction stays positive; otherwise the thresholds would wrap.

Signed-off-by: OpenWrt <openwrt@example.org>
---

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
@@ -340,11 +340,10 @@
 		[FE_PSE_PORT_GDM4] = 2,
 		[FE_PSE_PORT_CDM5] = 2,
 	};
+	u32 all_rsv, fq_limit, gdm4_rsv;
 	int q;
 
 	if (airoha_ppe_is_enabled(eth, 1)) {
-		u32 all_rsv;
-
 		/* hw misses PPE2 oq rsv */
 		all_rsv = airoha_fe_get_pse_all_rsv(eth);
 		all_rsv += PSE_RSV_PAGES *
@@ -399,10 +398,30 @@
 							 q, 0);
 		}
 	}
-	/* GDM4 */
+	/* GDM4. On the AN7581 this is the second 10G port, but the table above
+	 * only gives it two queues, so the stock per-queue reserve leaves it
+	 * with 16 KiB of guaranteed buffer for a port that can deliver at
+	 * 10G. Keep the queue count (it is a hardware property) and give those
+	 * queues a deeper reserve instead.
+	 *
+	 * The reserve feeds the shared-pool thresholds, which are computed as
+	 * fq_limit - all_rsv - <headroom>: reserving more than the pool holds
+	 * would underflow them, so raise the reserve only as far as the pool
+	 * actually allows.
+	 */
+	fq_limit = airoha_fe_get(eth, PSE_FQ_CFG, PSE_FQ_LIMIT_MASK);
+	all_rsv = airoha_fe_get_pse_all_rsv(eth);
+	gdm4_rsv = PSE_QUEUE_RSV_PAGES;
+	if (fq_limit > all_rsv + 0x400) {
+		u32 extra = (fq_limit - all_rsv - 0x400) /
+			    pse_port_num_queues[FE_PSE_PORT_GDM4];
+
+		if (extra > PSE_QUEUE_RSV_PAGES * 3)
+			extra = PSE_QUEUE_RSV_PAGES * 3;
+		gdm4_rsv += extra;
+	}
 	for (q = 0; q < pse_port_num_queues[FE_PSE_PORT_GDM4]; q++)
-		airoha_fe_set_pse_oq_rsv(eth, FE_PSE_PORT_GDM4, q,
-					 PSE_QUEUE_RSV_PAGES);
+		airoha_fe_set_pse_oq_rsv(eth, FE_PSE_PORT_GDM4, q, gdm4_rsv);
 	/* CDM5 */
 	for (q = 0; q < pse_port_num_queues[FE_PSE_PORT_CDM5]; q++)
 		airoha_fe_set_pse_oq_rsv(eth, FE_PSE_PORT_CDM5, q,
